Package: rasch
Type: Package
Title: Models and Diagnostics for Rasch Measurement Theory
Version: 1.12.0
Authors@R: person("Josh", "McGrane", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "drjoshmcgrane@gmail.com")
Description: Fits and evaluates the models of Rasch Measurement Theory
    (Rasch, 1960 <ISBN:9780226705538>; Andrich and Marais, 2019
    <doi:10.1007/978-981-13-7496-8>): the dichotomous Rasch, partial
    credit, rating scale, and many-facet models, the extended frame of
    reference model (Humphry, 2005; Humphry and Andrich, 2008), and
    comparative judgement models for dichotomous pairwise comparisons --
    the conditional form of the dichotomous model (Andrich, 1978
    <doi:10.1177/014662167800200319>) -- and polytomous pairwise
    comparisons (Tutz, 1986 <doi:10.1016/0022-2496(86)90034-9>). Item
    parameters are estimated by pairwise conditional maximum likelihood
    (Zwinderman, 1995 <doi:10.1177/014662169501900406>), with person
    measurement by weighted likelihood (Warm, 1989
    <doi:10.1007/BF02294627>). Functions are provided for fit, targeting,
    reliability, dimensionality, local dependence, differential item
    functioning, equating, and simulation. A point-and-click 'shiny' app
    provides the full functionality of the package.
URL: https://drjoshmcgrane.github.io/rasch/, https://github.com/drjoshmcgrane/rasch
BugReports: https://github.com/drjoshmcgrane/rasch/issues
